Alembic is the schema authority.

`app/db/session.py::init_db()` still exists, but it only runs when the database
URL is SQLite — it creates missing tables for local development and for the
test suite, and it can never alter an existing one. Anything with real data in
it is migrated:

    alembic upgrade head          # apply everything outstanding
    alembic current               # what the database thinks it is
    alembic history --verbose     # what exists
    alembic revision -m "..."     # a new, hand-written revision
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."

Autogenerate compares the database against `Base.metadata`, so a model that is
not re-exported from `app/models/__init__.py` is invisible to it and will be
proposed for deletion. Read every autogenerated revision before applying it.

The deploy runs `alembic upgrade head` before restarting the service, which is
safe only for additive migrations. A migration that drops or rewrites a column
the running code still uses needs the old code stopped first.
